<Base title="Terms of Service" description="ConnectFlow terms of service (draft).">
  <div class="wrap page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Terms of Service</h1></div>
  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <div class="callout">Draft for review. This text is a starting template and must be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before ConnectFlow is offered to the public.</div>
      <h2>1. The service</h2>
      <p>ConnectFlow provides software for researching leads, drafting messages and sending WhatsApp messages from numbers you link to your workspace.</p>
      <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may message only people with whom you have a lawful basis to communicate, and you must honour opt-out requests. You must not send spam, illegal, deceptive, harassing or abusive content, and you must comply with WhatsApp’s terms and the laws of your market.</p>
      <h2>3. WhatsApp connectivity</h2>
      <p>ConnectFlow is not affiliated with WhatsApp or Meta and is not the official WhatsApp Business API. WhatsApp may restrict or ban numbers. You accept this risk and are responsible for the numbers you link.</p>
      <h2>4. Accounts and billing</h2>
      <p>You are responsible for activity in your workspace. Paid plans renew monthly until cancelled. We may suspend workspaces that violate these terms.</p>
      <h2>5. Liability</h2>
      <p>The service is provided “as is”. To the extent permitted by law, ConnectFlow is not liable for indirect losses, including loss of a WhatsApp number or business opportunity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
